he formula?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81ab6a811ad468a318f3ce1cabbf79fac6470bb34f6f35f7d0ae85c8fb40b982" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂Q"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂y"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂z"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "∂g,\\text{ }Q,\\text{ }∂y"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "∂g,\\text{ }Q,\\text{ }∂z"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z={e}^{x}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x})={e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩{|}_{z={e}^{x}} \\\\  & =⟨{{y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x+{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{0}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y\\cdot ({e}^{x})-(x+{e}^{x})\\cdot 0+0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-y{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[-\\frac{{y}^{2}{e}^{x}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{[{e}^{x}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81ab6a811ad468a318f3ce1cabbf79fac6470bb34f6f35f7d0ae85c8fb40b982" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3e+{e}^{-1}}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{5e+2{e}^{-1}}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3e-{e}^{-1}}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7e-{e}^{-1}}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-x-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x-y)=-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x-y)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩{|}_{z=-x-y} \\\\  & =⟨{{{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{{e}^{y}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{1-x-y}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-({e}^{x})\\cdot (-1)-({e}^{y})\\cdot (-1)+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({e}^{x}+{e}^{y}+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}+{e}^{y}+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{e}^{x}y+{e}^{y}+y-xy-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}+e+1-x-\\frac{1}{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-x-\\frac{1}{2}+e)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{e}^{x}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{x}{2}+ex]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =e-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}+e-1 \\\\  & =2e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81ab6a811ad468a318f3ce1cabbf79fac6470bb34f6f35f7d0ae85c8fb40b982" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069555/state.json" "file_sha256" "9688e39da05c2ddc3a1115d98aa05fedaa658a524f97a566033103326a47863d" "basis" 2390 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivaria